 ends; <a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"5063272746861264748\"><a href=\"#5063272746861264748\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x4864\" person=\"x4864\" title=\"Luman Hopkins Calkins\">Luman H. Corkins Calkins</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Calkins, Luman Hopkins\"><p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/luman-hopkins-calkins\">View Full Bio</a></p></div></div></aside> say</td> <td xml:id=\"X83741\">2 days. labor</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83742\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"2174028590431371371\"><a href=\"#2174028590431371371\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans45\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> handwriting ends; handwriting presumably of subscribers begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"2212694611706002962\"><a href=\"#2212694611706002962\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per1085\" person=\"per1085\" title=\"Albern Allen\">Albern Allen</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Allen, Albern\"><p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/albern-allen\">View Full Bio</a></p></div></div></aside> says</td> <td xml:id=\"X83744\">2 days labors W. Joseph Young</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83745\">John Binley says</td> <td xml:id=\"X83746\">2 days labors <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"2333175609962748744\"><a href=\"#2333175609962748744\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans10\"><span id=\"documenttrans10\">10</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Possibly “Trum Angel,” meaning <a href=\"/person/truman-osborn-angell\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Truman O. Angell</a>, who directed the joiner work on the <a href=\"/place/nauvoo-illinois\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Nauvoo</a> <a href=\"/place/temple-nauvoo-illinois\" class=\"referenceInPop\">temple</a> under architect <a href=\"/person/william-weeks\" class=\"referenceInPop\">William Weeks</a>. (Angell, Autobiography, 20.)</p><hr><div class=\"works-cited-links\"><a href=\"/works-cited\" class=\"pdf\" id=\"comp-works\">Comprehensive Works Cited</a></div><div class=\"source-note\"><p id=\"source-note1\"> Angell, Truman O. Autobiography, 1884. CHL. MS 12334. Also available in Archie Leon Brown and Charlene L. Hathaway, <span class=\"title\">141 Years of Mormon Heritage: Rawsons, Browns, Angells—Pioneers</span> (Oakland, CA: By the authors, 1973), 119–135. </p></div></div></div></aside></td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83748\">F. P. Richards— says</td> <td xml:id=\"X83749\">3 days with Team</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83750\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"11880033038443593577\"><a href=\"#11880033038443593577\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per333\" person=\"per333\" title=\"Hugh McFall\">Hugh McFall</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"McFall, Hugh\"><p>Ca. 1798–after 1860. Carpenter. Born in Pennsylvania. Married Elizabeth. Moved to Ohio, by 1834. Moved to Illinois, by 1839. Lived at Hancock Co., Illinois, 1840. Appointed adjutant general in Nauvoo Legion, 9 Mar. 1841, in Nauvoo, Hancock Co. Member of Nauvoo...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/hugh-mcfall\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside></td> <td xml:id=\"X83751\">$1— in produce</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83752\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"4130120626399657356\"><a href=\"#4130120626399657356\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per159\" person=\"per159\" title=\"Hosea Stout\">Hosea Stout</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Stout, Hosea\"><p>18 Sept. 1810–2 Mar. 1889. Farmer, teacher, carpenter, sawmill operator, lawyer. Born near Pleasant Hill, Mercer Co., Kentucky. Son of Joseph Stout and Anna Smith. Moved to Union Township, Clinton Co., Ohio, 1819; to Wilmington, Clinton Co., fall 1824; to...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/hosea-stout\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside></td> <td xml:id=\"X83753\">2.00 paid<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"13341068474190176257\"><a href=\"#13341068474190176257\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans46\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of <a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a>.</p><hr></div></div></aside></td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83755\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"4700924963541169920\"><a href=\"#4700924963541169920\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x114526\" person=\"x114526\" title=\"Thomas Woolsey\">Tho<span class=\"underscore\">s</span> Woolsey</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Woolsey, Thomas\"><p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/thomas-woolsey\">View Full Bio</a></p></div></div></aside></td> <td xml:id=\"X83756\">5.00 in stone</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83757\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"1911617351367393376\"><a href=\"#1911617351367393376\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x114530\" person=\"x114530\" title=\"Wesley Knight\">Wesley Knight</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Knight, Wesley\"><p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/wesley-knight\">View Full Bio</a></p></div></div></aside></td> <td xml:id=\"X83758\">1-00 in wheet</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83759\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"15404513989081289635\"><a href=\"#15404513989081289635\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans47\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Handwriting presumably of subscribers ends; <a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"17233270625332981696\"><a href=\"#17233270625332981696\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per1181\" person=\"per1181\" title=\"Sylvester Emmons\">Sylvester Emmons</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Emmons, Sylvester\"><p>28 Feb. 1808–15 Nov. 1881. Lawyer, newspaper editor/publisher. Born in Readington Township, Hunterdon Co., New Jersey. Son of Abraham Emmons and Margaret Vlerebome. Moved to Philadelphia, 1831. Moved to Illinois, 1840. Admitted to bar in Hancock Co., Illinois...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/sylvester-emmons\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside>—</td> <td xml:id=\"X83761\">$1,00. Paid</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83762\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"5615137722418788658\"><a href=\"#5615137722418788658\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans48\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> handwriting ends; handwriting presumably of subscriber begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16307101011999484594\"><a href=\"#16307101011999484594\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x4431\" person=\"x4431\" title=\"Benjamin Warrington\">Benjamin Warrington</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Warrington, Benjamin\"><p>1810–June 1850. Wheelwright. Born in New Jersey. Married Sarah Horner, 16 Jan. 1834, in Preble Co., Ohio. Owned lots in Somerville, Milford Township, Butler Co., Ohio, 1835–ca. 1838. Moved to Hancock Co., Illinois, by 1840. Appointed quartermaster sergeant...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/benjamin-warrington\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside></td> <td xml:id=\"X83764\">$100 in produce</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83765\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"15250537880266753997\"><a href=\"#15250537880266753997\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans49\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Handwriting presumably of subscriber ends; <a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"7394684550416719271\"><a href=\"#7394684550416719271\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per896\" person=\"per896\" title=\"Micah Baldwin Welton\">Micah B. Welton</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Welton, Micah Baldwin\"><p>13 Aug. 1792–9 Aug. 1861. Carpenter. Born in Waterbury, New Haven Co., Connecticut. Son of Eliakim Welton III and Loly Barnes. Married first Wealthy Upson. Moved to Medina, Medina Co., Ohio, by 1820. Married second Rebecca Smith, 3 Mar. 1828, in Portage Co...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/micah-baldwin-welton\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside> says</td> <td xml:id=\"X83767\">$2,00 Labor Joiner.—</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83768\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"3794025662736909208\"><a href=\"#3794025662736909208\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x115072\" person=\"x115072\" title=\"Thomas Evans\">Thomas Evans</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Evans, Thomas\"><p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/thomas-evans\">View Full Bio</a></p></div></div></aside> says.</td> <td xml:id=\"X83769\">carpenter or sawyer— 1 day</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83770\">Thomas Preece— says</td> <td xml:id=\"X83771\">Sawyer 1 day</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83772\">Hiram C Jacobs says</td> <td xml:id=\"X83773\">25 bushels lime Mortar</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83774\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"17679566152835536178\"><a href=\"#17679566152835536178\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x4561\" person=\"x4561\" title=\"Edward Robinson\">Edward Robinson</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Robinson, Edward\"><p>2 Aug. 1819–20 Nov. 1861. Oculist (ophthalmologist). Born in England. Immigrated to U.S., before June 1844. Resident of Marion Co., Illinois, by June 1850. Married Mary Truitt, 6 Nov. 1853, in Greene Co., Illinois. Moved to Greenville, Bond Co., Illinois,...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/edward-robinson\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside> says</td> <td xml:id=\"X83775\">$5,00</td> </tr> </tbody></table> <div class=\"noindent wasptag\"> [p. [9]]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><table width=\"100%\"> <tbody><tr> <td xml:id=\"X83733\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10818024001706334993\"><a href=\"#10818024001706334993\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans42\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Handwriting presumably of subscribers ends; <a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"4049082798280026076\"><a href=\"#4049082798280026076\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per529\" person=\"per529\" title=\"Ephraim Potter\">Ephraim <span class=\"deleted\">E.</span> Potter</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Potter, Ephraim\"><p>7 June 1817–after Sept. 1845. Born in Monmouth Co., New Jersey. Son of Ephraim Potter and Hannah Woodmansee. Moved to Nauvoo, Hancock Co., Illinois, by July 1841. Member of Nauvoo Legion. Baptized into Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints and left ...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/ephraim-potter\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside>. say</td> <td xml:id=\"X83734\">$3.00. in lumber when obtained from &lt;​H. H.​&gt;</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83736\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"13359409278905914158\"><a href=\"#13359409278905914158\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans43\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> handwriting ends; handwriting presumably of subscriber begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside>W<span class=\"superscript\">m.</span> S Walters</td> <td xml:id=\"X83738\">1, @</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83739\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"4603331224310227676\"><a href=\"#4603331224310227676\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans44\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Handwriting presumably of subscriber ends; <a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"9028800549288270250\"><a href=\"#9028800549288270250\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x4864\" person=\"x4864\" title=\"Luman Hopkins Calkins\">Luman H. Corkins [Calkins]</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Calkins, Luman Hopkins\"><p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/luman-hopkins-calkins\">View Full Bio</a></p></div></div></aside> say</td> <td xml:id=\"X83741\">2 days. labor</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83742\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"3499928017020036554\"><a href=\"#3499928017020036554\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans45\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> handwriting ends; handwriting presumably of subscribers begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16749623616370663484\"><a href=\"#16749623616370663484\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per1085\" person=\"per1085\" title=\"Albern Allen\">Albe[r]n Allen</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Allen, Albern\"><p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/albern-allen\">View Full Bio</a></p></div></div></aside> says</td> <td xml:id=\"X83744\">2 days labors &lt;​W. Joseph Young​&gt;</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83745\">John Binley says</td> <td xml:id=\"X83746\">2 days labors &lt;​<span class=\"illegible\">[2 words illegible]</span>​&gt;<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16316063919767906622\"><a href=\"#16316063919767906622\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans10\"><span id=\"documenttrans10\">10</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Possibly “Trum Angel,” meaning <a href=\"/person/truman-osborn-angell\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Truman O. Angell</a>, who directed the joiner work on the <a href=\"/place/nauvoo-illinois\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Nauvoo</a> <a href=\"/place/temple-nauvoo-illinois\" class=\"referenceInPop\">temple</a> under architect <a href=\"/person/william-weeks\" class=\"referenceInPop\">William Weeks</a>. (Angell, Autobiography, 20.)</p><hr><div class=\"works-cited-links\"><a href=\"/works-cited\" class=\"pdf\" id=\"comp-works\">Comprehensive Works Cited</a></div><div class=\"source-note\"><p id=\"source-note1\"> Angell, Truman O. Autobiography, 1884. CHL. MS 12334. Also available in Archie Leon Brown and Charlene L. Hathaway, <span class=\"title\">141 Years of Mormon Heritage: Rawsons, Browns, Angells—Pioneers</span> (Oakland, CA: By the authors, 1973), 119–135. </p></div></div></div></aside></td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83748\">F. P. Richards— says</td> <td xml:id=\"X83749\">3 days with Team</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83750\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"5561912838222892943\"><a href=\"#5561912838222892943\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per333\" person=\"per333\" title=\"Hugh McFall\">Hugh M<span class=\"superscript\">c</span>Fall</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"McFall, Hugh\"><p>Ca. 1798–after 1860. Carpenter. Born in Pennsylvania. Married Elizabeth. Moved to Ohio, by 1834. Moved to Illinois, by 1839. Lived at Hancock Co., Illinois, 1840. Appointed adjutant general in Nauvoo Legion, 9 Mar. 1841, in Nauvoo, Hancock Co. Member of Nauvoo...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/hugh-mcfall\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside></td> <td xml:id=\"X83751\">$1— in produce</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83752\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"5571566788803387190\"><a href=\"#5571566788803387190\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per159\" person=\"per159\" title=\"Hosea Stout\">Hosea Stout</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Stout, Hosea\"><p>18 Sept. 1810–2 Mar. 1889. Farmer, teacher, carpenter, sawmill operator, lawyer. Born near Pleasant Hill, Mercer Co., Kentucky. Son of Joseph Stout and Anna Smith. Moved to Union Township, Clinton Co., Ohio, 1819; to Wilmington, Clinton Co., fall 1824; to...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/hosea-stout\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside></td> <td xml:id=\"X83753\">2.00 &lt;​paid​&gt;<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"15482774805632243266\"><a href=\"#15482774805632243266\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans46\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of <a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a>.</p><hr></div></div></aside></td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83755\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"3607172775124197096\"><a href=\"#3607172775124197096\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x114526\" person=\"x114526\" title=\"Thomas Woolsey\">Tho<span class=\"superscript\"><span class=\"underscore\">s</span></span> Woolsey</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Woolsey, Thomas\"><p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/thomas-woolsey\">View Full Bio</a></p></div></div></aside></td> <td xml:id=\"X83756\">5.00 in stone</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83757\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"4340471778272109820\"><a href=\"#4340471778272109820\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x114530\" person=\"x114530\" title=\"Wesley Knight\">W[esley] Knight</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Knight, Wesley\"><p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/wesley-knight\">View Full Bio</a></p></div></div></aside></td> <td xml:id=\"X83758\">1-00 in wheet</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83759\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"11800222480009528902\"><a href=\"#11800222480009528902\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans47\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Handwriting presumably of subscribers ends; <a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10170928073693805686\"><a href=\"#10170928073693805686\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per1181\" person=\"per1181\" title=\"Sylvester Emmons\">S[ylvester] Emmons</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Emmons, Sylvester\"><p>28 Feb. 1808–15 Nov. 1881. Lawyer, newspaper editor/publisher. Born in Readington Township, Hunterdon Co., New Jersey. Son of Abraham Emmons and Margaret Vlerebome. Moved to Philadelphia, 1831. Moved to Illinois, 1840. Admitted to bar in Hancock Co., Illinois...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/sylvester-emmons\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside>—</td> <td xml:id=\"X83761\">$1,00. &lt;​Paid​&gt;</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83762\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"1458810921381619845\"><a href=\"#1458810921381619845\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans48\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> handwriting ends; handwriting presumably of subscriber begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16481770448408726490\"><a href=\"#16481770448408726490\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x4431\" person=\"x4431\" title=\"Benjamin Warrington\">B[enjamin] Warrington</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Warrington, Benjamin\"><p>1810–June 1850. Wheelwright. Born in New Jersey. Married Sarah Horner, 16 Jan. 1834, in Preble Co., Ohio. Owned lots in Somerville, Milford Township, Butler Co., Ohio, 1835–ca. 1838. Moved to Hancock Co., Illinois, by 1840. Appointed quartermaster sergeant...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/benjamin-warrington\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside></td> <td xml:id=\"X83764\">$100 in produce</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83765\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"6911960665497961037\"><a href=\"#6911960665497961037\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans49\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Handwriting presumably of subscriber ends; <a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"133950360504980676\"><a href=\"#133950360504980676\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per896\" person=\"per896\" title=\"Micah Baldwin Welton\">M[icah] B. Welton</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Welton, Micah Baldwin\"><p>13 Aug. 1792–9 Aug. 1861. Carpenter. Born in Waterbury, New Haven Co., Connecticut. Son of Eliakim Welton III and Loly Barnes. Married first Wealthy Upson. Moved to Medina, Medina Co., Ohio, by 1820. Married second Rebecca Smith, 3 Mar. 1828, in Portage Co...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/micah-baldwin-welton\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside> says</td> <td xml:id=\"X83767\">$2,00 Labor Joiner.—</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83768\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"17085523997460080102\"><a href=\"#17085523997460080102\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x115072\" person=\"x115072\" title=\"Thomas Evans\">Thomas Evans</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Evans, Thomas\"><p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/thomas-evans\">View Full Bio</a></p></div></div></aside> says.</td> <td xml:id=\"X83769\">carpenter or sawyer— 1 day</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83770\">Thomas Preece— says</td> <td xml:id=\"X83771\">Sawyer 1 day</td> </tr> <tr> <td xm